1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Sultanate of Rûm===
2 CONT
2 CONT Kutalmish was the son of Arslan Yabgu and a cousin of Tughril and played a vital role in the conquests of the Seljuq Turks. He supported a rebellion against Tughril and contested the succession to the throne with Alp Arslan. Accor
2 CONC ding to the historian Ali ibn al-Athir, Kutalmish knew the sciences of the stars.[1] His son, Suleiman, was appointed Sultan of Rûm by Malik Shah I in 1073.
