2 CONC ng the turbulent Turkish troops from the city to quarters outside of it, before dying in 490/1097.  His good reputation was such that his tomb later became a place of pilgrimage (Moḥammad b. Ebrāhim, pp. 20-21; Afżal-al-Din Kermān
