2 CONT https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=pt&u=https://gw.geneanet.org/aqf%3Flang%3Den%26p%3Dpedro%2Bpires%2Bde%26n%3Dportel&prev=search&pto=aue
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Vaspurakan (also transliterated as Vasbouragan from Western Armenian; Armenian: Վասպուրական, (Vaspourakan) meaning the "noble land" or "land of princes"[1]) was the eighth province of the ancient kingdom of Armenia, which later be
2 CONC came an independent kingdom during the Middle Ages, centered on Lake Van. Located in what is now southeastern Turkey and northwestern Iran, the region is considered to be the cradle of Armenian civilization.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaspurakan
2 CONT ----
