2 CONT '''Alda or Alde was an 11th-century Alan princess and the second wife of King George I of Georgia (r. 1014–1027)'''. The couple had a son, Demetre, who played a notable role in the civil unrest of Georgia during the reign of his h
2 CONC alf-brother Bagrat IV.[1]   
