1 NOTE RBS :  Adarnase IV of Tao, King of K'art'li was the son of Davit' I of Tao, Kuropalati and N. N. Arcruni.1,2,3 The Bagratuni dynasty divided in the 9th century into two branches,one which reigned in Armenia, starting with Ashot I 
2 CONC in 885, and the other of which reigned in Iberia, starting with Adarnese II in 888. The Armenian branch ceded Armenia to the Byzantine Empire in 1045, while Iberia united with Abkhazeti (Abkhazia) and became known as Georgia, taki
2 CONC ng its name from King Giorgi I (1014-1027). Adarnase IV of Tao, King of K'art'li was son of Davit. Also called Atrnerseh of Iberia. He was the successor of Davit' I of Tao, Kuropalati; (48th) curopalates. Adarnase IV of Tao, King 
2 CONC of K'art'li restored the monarchy of Iberia in 888. He was of the Bagratid branch of the Tayk' (Tao) lineage, based near the borders between Armenia and Georgia along the river Djorokh (Coruh), and created the Iberian kingdom of t
2 CONC he Bagratids in 888. 49th King of Kartli at Transcaucasia between 888 and 923. Curopalate between 891 and 923.
