1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=13065 '''Li Tao''' 李濤] [13065] He fled with his father at the end of Tang. He became Hengyang ling under the Ma ruler of Chu, but when his elder cousin, Yu(10) [1
2 CONC 9565], took office under the Liang and Hou Tang, he traveled north and served Liang and was a chief minister under Later Jin and Han and was appointed Bingbu shangshu by Song Taizu. However, the only notice of his posts as chief m
2 CONC inister are under the Later Han. His son remained behind in Xiangtan since he traveled alone to the North. See Su Song's inscription for his descendant, Chang [971]. Wan Sitong, Wudai Jiangxiang dachen nianpu (ERWSBB), p. 8. CBD, 
2 CONC 2, 919-20.From Hartwell's ACTIVITY table:947:  Apt. Hanlin xueshi, Hubu shangshu, Zhongshu shilang (State Council)948:  Dismissed (ba) from State Council.                                                                            
2 CONC                                                                                                      ndant Li(2) Bing [8082], locates them in Caozhou, Jiyin (modern Caoxian) county until Jinggui, who moved to Jizhou, Juye county. 
2 CONC I identify Tao(5) as making the move, but it probably took place much earlier. CBD, 2, 919-20. 《唐代人物知識ベース》記其生卒年為：898 - 961. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
