2 DATE 631
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 630 – 631 Prédécesseur	Bûrândûkht Successeur	Azarmedûkht Biographie Dynastie	Mihranides Date de décès	631 Père	Schahr-Barâz Mère	Mirhrān, sœur de Khosro II
2 CONT
2 CONT Fils de l'usurpateur Schahr-Barâz, et vraisemblablement de la princesse Mirhrān, une sœur de Khosro II1, il tente en vain de s'imposer en 630/631 après la destitution de la reine Bûrândûkht avec l'appui de Farrukh Hormizd, mais il
2 CONC  doit faire face aux candidats « sassanides légitimes » au trône, Khosro III et Péroz II, et surtout Azarmedûkht, la sœur de Bûrândûkht soutenue par le parti des « Pārsig »
2 CONT
2 CONT Shapur-i Shahrvaraz was the son of Shahrbaraz, the famous Sasanian spahbed and briefly shahanshah. His mother was the sister of Khosrau II.[1] In 630, after Borandukht was deposed, Shapur became king of the Sasanian Empire but was
2 CONC  shortly deposed by the Sasanian nobles who did not acknowledge his rule. He was succeeded by his cousin Azarmidokht. When she became queen of Persia, Farrukh Hormizd proposed to marry her, which Shapur was in favor of; however, A
2 CONC zarmidokht declined the proposal and became angry at Shapur for agreeing.[2] What happened to Shapur afterward is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as Shapur V, was an Sasanian usurper who reigned for a short time in 630 until he was deposed in favor of Azarmidokht.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Shapur-i Shahrvaraz (Middle Persian: 𐭱𐭧𐭯𐭥𐭧𐭥𐭩𐭩 𐭧𐭱𐭨𐭥𐭥𐭥𐭰), also known as Shapur V, was a Sasanian usurper who reigned for a short time in 630 until he was deposed in favor of Azarmidokht.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shapur-i Shahrvaraz was the son of Shahrbaraz, the famous Sasanian spahbed and briefly shahanshah. His mother was the sister of Khosrau II, Mehran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 630, after Borandukht was deposed, Shapur became king of the Sasanian Empire but was shortly deposed by the Sasanian nobles who did not acknowledge his rule. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his cousin Azarmidokht. When she became queen of Persia, Farrukh Hormizd proposed to marry her, which Shapur was in favor of; however, Azarmidokht declined the proposal and became angry at Shapur for agreeing.
2 CONT
2 CONT What happened to Shapur afterward is not known.
