2 CONT "Toghrul Shah . Muhammad Shah Seljuq, King of Kerman, died at Jiruft A.H. 545 (1169-1170), and left four sons, Turan Shah, Bahram Shah, Arsland Shah,  and Turkan Shah, who immediately after their father’s death fought with one ano
2 CONC ther for the throne. Turan and Bahram had the same mother, Khatun Rukni, a Seljuq princess, who died A.H. 577 (1181). Turan was killed in 579 (1183), in Kerman, by Zafir Muhammag, on of Atabeg Qutb al din Muhammad’s (d. 22nd Nover
2 CONC mber, 1186) officers; Bahram died A.H. 570 (1174-1175), of dropsy; and Arslan met his death A.H. 572 (1176-1177) in an engagement against the Turkish Amir Aibek. Turkan was killed by his brother Bahram in 565 (1170). The last of t
2 CONC he Kerman Seljuqs was Bahram Shah’s son Muhammad Shah, who succeeded to the throne in 1183, and fled to the Ghuris in 1187 on the arrival of Malik Dinar. "
