2 CONT * “Armenia: Art, Religion, and Trade in the Middle Ages.” By Helen C. Evans, Constance Alchermes, Ina Baghdiantz McCabe, Anna Ballian, Sheila R. Canby, Kathrin Colburn, Yolande Crowe, Michael Daniel Findikyan, Rachel Goshgarian, G
2 CONC rigor Grigoryan, Zsuzsanna Gulácsi, Asoghik Karapetian, Anna Leyloyan-Yekmalyan, Christina Maranci, Sylvie L. Merian, Erin Piñon, Earnestine M. Qiu, Ioanna Rapti, Joanna Rydzkowska-Kozak, Suzan Yalman.  [https://books.google.com/b
2 CONC ooks?id=ezNtDwAAQBAJ&lpg=PA78&ots=hoZB3inz60&dq=Ashot%20II%20the%20Iron%2C%20king%20of%20Armenia&pg=PA78#v=snippet&q=Ashot%20II%20the%20Iron,%20king%20of%20Armenia&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * [https://www.degruyter.com/view/PMBZ/PMBZ22799?rskey=cSkJYW&result=4&dbq_0=Ashot&dbf_0=pmbz-fulltext&dbt_0=fulltext&o_0=AND “ Ašot II. “The Iron” (from Armenia)] V: Armenian king from the Bagratid family. Son of King Smbat I, “t
2 CONC he martyr” ( # 27141 ), brother of Abas I ( # 20006 ), grandson of King Asot I “the great” of Armenia.   His successor was his brother Abas.
