2 CONT Arslan Shah I was Sultan of Kerman (1101–1142), a city in Iran situated at the center of Kerman province. Located in a large and flat plain, this city is placed 1,076 km (669 mi) south of the Iranian capital, Tehran.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arslan Shah I (1101–1142) was preceded by Iran Shah (1096–1101) and was succeeded by Mehmed I (Muhammad) (1142–1156).
