1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theodora Megale Komnene (Greek: Θεοδώρα Μεγάλη Κομνηνή, Theodōra Megalē Komnēnē), (before 1253– after 1285), Empress of Trebizond from 1284 to 1285. She was a daughter of Emperor Manuel I of Trebizond by his second
2 CONC  wife, Rusudan, a Georgian princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1284, with help of Georgian King of Imereti, David VI Narin she managed to seize the crown from her half-brother, Emperor John II. Shortly afterwards she was defeated and John regained his throne, but she had managed reign long
2 CONC  enough to have minted her own coins. Either before or after her short reign, Theodora was a nun.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT [Emperor Manuel I & his second [wife] had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         THEODORA Komnene (-after [1285]).  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records "the attack, raid and sudden flight of the lady Theodora Komnene, the first daughter of the lord Manuel the Grand Komnenos by Russadan from I
2 CONC beria", dated to [1283/85] from the context[29].  She succeeded her brother in [1284/85] as THEODORA Empress in Trebizond.  The existence of 36 specimens of coins struck during her reign confirms that this laconic passage in Micha
2 CONC el Panaretos indicates that Theodora ruled as empress for a brief period, although the circumstances of her succession and flight are unknown] ref: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TREBIZOND.htm#AlexiosITrebizondB
